# Keep the build context to what the image actually needs.
#
# THIS FILE IS LOAD-BEARING, not housekeeping. The Dockerfile installs clean
# dependencies in the `deps` stage and copies them forward, and then `COPY . .`
# in the builder stage copies the build context over the top. Without
# node_modules excluded here, whatever happens to be on the build host's disk
# silently replaces the tree npm ci just resolved from the lockfile — so the
# image ships the host's dependencies and the lockfile is decorative. That is
# exactly how a patched Next release was built into an image that still
# contained the vulnerable one.
node_modules
.next

# Runtime state. data/ is a bind mount in compose, so a copy baked into the
# image would only ever be a stale shadow of it.
data
shots

# Secrets. Compose reads .env.local on the host and passes the values in at
# run time; nothing here is needed to build, and a credential baked into an
# image layer outlives any attempt to remove it.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Not part of the application.
.git
.gitignore
.github
.claude
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose*.yml
README.md
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
npm-debug.log*
.DS_Store
